  "agent": {
    "note": "**The DSL string no longer crams — long strings PAGE to follow the parse.** Same 8×8 from your last shot; the 154-char string now stays legible.\n\n**How (and the engine reality behind it):** I first tried a true pixel-scroll and hit three hard walls, all verified:\n\n| Primitive | Result |\n|---|---|\n| source `overlay.xExpr` | animates, but drawtext only rasterizes to the cell width → off-cell glyphs are never drawn, scroll reveals blank |\n| per-layer `xExpr` | evaluated ONCE (static) — no animation |\n| camera crop | uniform zoom + upscales rasterized pixels → blurry text |\n\nSo smooth pixel-scroll isn't crisply available. Instead the window **pages**: the string is cut into hard-capped pages (~48 chars), each a crisp fixed strip, stacked as **enable-gated** layers — only the page holding the caret shows, advancing as the parse crosses a boundary. The cap is the hard upper limit you asked for; under it, nothing changes (still one strip).\n\n**Your SVG insight was the unlock.** Paging only toggles `overlay.enable` (show/hide) — no per-frame motion — so the SVG rasterizer's animation uncertainty never applies. I moved the glyphs to **`rasterizer: \"svg\"`**: faster than drawtext (as you said), crisper outlines, and exactly the static-content case it's built for. So paging didn't *cost* us SVG — it's what *enabled* it.\n\n*(Verified: the 8×8 string panel pages cleanly through all 154 chars — page 1 `8[8(F,F…`, later pages ruler `100…125` etc., caret + narration synced throughout. 156 tests green.)*\n\n**One honest caveat on this 8×8 render:** the heavy part is the CANVAS (one cursor ring per step → 154 rings on a 64-tile grid), not the string — that's the dense-layout cost already tracked in the overlay-depth `.ai` candidate, and it's the next thing to optimize. The string panel itself is light.",
    "question": "Does the paged DSL string read well on the 8×8 — legible window, advancing with the parse, crisp SVG glyphs? And is paging (vs smooth pixel-scroll) the right call given the engine limits above? If yes, M3 is complete and I'll move to **M4 (debugger)** — or tackle the canvas cursor-ring density first if you'd rather.",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "other",
        "label": "dsl-string-scroll"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "propose",
        "summary": "Long DSL strings page (enable-gated windows) instead of cramming; glyphs moved to the SVG rasterizer (faster/crisper, paging needs no per-frame animation)."
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "017"
      }
    }
  }
